{
  "scope": "Hero Mode roster: six forms per race, with Edmund Duke in his Siege Tank replacing Norad II. Raynor and Fenix each occupy separate slots for their distinct forms.",
  "stats": "Stock Brood War data before player upgrades. Intrinsic Fenix range and Devouring One attack-speed upgrade are included. Cooldown is nominal before the engine’s random variation and animation timing. Starting HP, campaign upgrades and map overrides can change in-mission values. Hero DAT costs are editor defaults, not actual build prices.",
  "pricing": "Hero Mode cost = regular unit cost × estimated equivalent-unit count × 2/3, rounded to the nearest 5 resources. Raynor Marine: 50 × 3 × 2/3 = 100 minerals, 0 gas. Equivalents mostly follow weapon output; casters and Carrier hulls use the stated role estimates. Extra durability does not add another premium. These are deliberately discounted starting prices, not measured multiplayer balance. One living unit of each form per player; normal counterpart supply; rebuilding after death allowed. Enabled only in optional Hero Mode for custom and multiplayer games. Queued heroes reserve their limit across every producer. Trained at Engineering Bays, Evolution Chambers and Forges; upgrades share their production time. Infested Duran requires a Lair/Hive and Hydralisk Den; Infested Kerrigan requires a Hive and Queen’s Nest. Other heroes require the counterpart’s production/tech buildings. Tassadar and Zeratul merge into the original hero Archon, reserving both slots until it dies. The Archon uses four supply and has 100 HP, 800 shields, 3 armor and 60 ground/air damage before upgrades.",
